From 80024668b369603fbe2b5e8c47a41334e5c3813d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:20:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Documents: Aurelia branding, and a plainer, fuller /guide
 front page

The /guide shell (all four documents) takes the consumer brand: the real
logo lockup, the mark's orange-to-gold gradient as a rule under the top
bar and on section headings, the soft #FFE682 glow from Home, and the
network artwork. The front page explains what each document is, what is
inside and who it is for, and no longer names a person. The playbook
gets the strongest treatment: logo, glow and artwork on the cover,
gradient milestone tiles and a closing mark. The standalone admin
guideline gets the logo and the gradient rules. Brand artwork is read
from src/assets by scripts/guides/brand.py, never redrawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
